d the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a24b403-754c-5424-8182-8cad3487deed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105488 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =13\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105489 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15607" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105489 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,3,-1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,-7,0 \\rangle.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105489 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da8a1521-86cc-5747-88a7-e2ec56010c11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105489 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-7)+(-1)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{53}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105490 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15608" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105490 #edb/ref 1071 "Let ![](images/e4/e477b14c9148f4132c747a358e1e99f76d40df85b82c66d6e7dd38581b33913c.png) and ![](images/b1/b17d86e3e395b2fd752f5529090c0a5e4e2fdce17642be5594bee98e8c47fed2.png) Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105490 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4693b28f-df75-574e-8e49-bb89e162b107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105490 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{c}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Angles and Magnitudes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105916 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/r